WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.002
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B two, Book one.

2
00:00:05.302 --> 00:00:09.292
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.592 --> 00:00:15.855
Unit one: Self-Expression. Today you will add extra information with relative clauses using 'which'.

4
00:00:16.155 --> 00:00:18.749
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:23.293
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:24.942
Voice.

7
00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:28.646
Voice means your own way of expressing ideas.

8
00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:31.749
Writing poems helps me find my voice.

9
00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:34.886
Your turn. Say: Voice.

10
00:00:37.733 --> 00:00:38.700
Voice.

11
00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:40.428
Perspective.

12
00:00:41.417 --> 00:00:43.799
Perspective means a way of seeing things.

13
00:00:44.383 --> 00:00:46.801
Every writer shares a different perspective.

14
00:00:47.417 --> 00:00:50.069
Your turn. Say: Perspective.

15
00:00:52.933 --> 00:00:54.004
Perspective.

16
00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:55.879
Creative writing.

17
00:00:56.883 --> 00:01:00.241
Creative writing means writing stories, poems or plays.

18
00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:02.733
I joined a creative writing club.

19
00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:06.420
Your turn. Say: Creative writing.

20
00:01:09.267 --> 00:01:10.581
Creative writing.

21
00:01:11.317 --> 00:01:12.910
Artistic expression.

22
00:01:13.917 --> 00:01:17.855
Artistic expression means showing ideas and feelings through art.

23
00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:21.552
Apsara dance is a beautiful artistic expression.

24
00:01:22.150 --> 00:01:25.151
Your turn. Say: Artistic expression.

25
00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:29.547
Artistic expression.

26
00:01:30.283 --> 00:01:31.679
Individuality.

27
00:01:32.683 --> 00:01:36.343
Individuality means the qualities that make you different from others.

28
00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:39.193
Her paintings show her individuality.

29
00:01:39.783 --> 00:01:42.865
Your turn. Say: Individuality.

30
00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:47.200
Individuality.

31
00:01:47.950 --> 00:01:49.230
Authenticity.

32
00:01:50.217 --> 00:01:53.075
Authenticity means being real and true to yourself.

33
00:01:53.683 --> 00:01:56.136
Readers love the authenticity of his stories.

34
00:01:56.750 --> 00:01:59.785
Your turn. Say: Authenticity.

35
00:02:02.633 --> 00:02:03.832
Authenticity.

36
00:02:04.583 --> 00:02:05.492
Narrative.

37
00:02:06.483 --> 00:02:09.179
Narrative means a story or an account of events.

38
00:02:09.783 --> 00:02:11.736
The film has a powerful narrative.

39
00:02:12.350 --> 00:02:14.979
Your turn. Say: Narrative.

40
00:02:17.833 --> 00:02:18.927
Narrative.

41
00:02:19.683 --> 00:02:20.893
Symbolism.

42
00:02:21.883 --> 00:02:25.160
Symbolism means using objects to stand for ideas.

43
00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:28.435
The lotus is full of symbolism in Khmer art.

44
00:02:29.050 --> 00:02:32.062
Your turn. Say: Symbolism.

45
00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:35.959
Symbolism.

46
00:02:36.717 --> 00:02:37.590
Medium.

47
00:02:38.583 --> 00:02:41.895
Medium means a material or way used to create art.

48
00:02:42.483 --> 00:02:44.715
Watercolour is my favourite medium.

49
00:02:45.317 --> 00:02:47.470
Your turn. Say: Medium.

50
00:02:50.333 --> 00:02:51.102
Medium.

51
00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:53.130
Interpretation.

52
00:02:54.117 --> 00:02:57.289
Interpretation means your own understanding of a meaning.

53
00:02:57.883 --> 00:03:00.974
My interpretation of the poem is different from yours.

54
00:03:01.583 --> 00:03:04.294
Your turn. Say: Interpretation.

55
00:03:07.133 --> 00:03:08.436
Interpretation.

56
00:03:09.183 --> 00:03:10.451
Originality.

57
00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:14.285
Originality means being new and not copied.

58
00:03:14.883 --> 00:03:17.080
The judges praised her originality.

59
00:03:17.683 --> 00:03:20.289
Your turn. Say: Originality.

60
00:03:23.133 --> 00:03:24.401
Originality.

61
00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:26.395
Inspiration.

62
00:03:27.383 --> 00:03:30.509
Inspiration means something that gives you new ideas.

63
00:03:31.117 --> 00:03:33.395
Nature is my greatest inspiration.

64
00:03:33.983 --> 00:03:36.531
Your turn. Say: Inspiration.

65
00:03:39.367 --> 00:03:40.530
Inspiration.

66
00:03:41.333 --> 00:03:45.135
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:45.983 --> 00:03:49.051
Visal, how do you express yourself creatively?

68
00:03:50.150 --> 00:03:54.007
Creative writing, which I started last year, gives me a voice.

69
00:03:55.117 --> 00:03:56.524
What do you write about?

70
00:03:57.617 --> 00:04:02.661
Short narratives. I use symbolism, like the lotus, to show hope.

71
00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:07.645
That shows real originality. Where do you find inspiration?

72
00:04:08.750 --> 00:04:12.909
In my grandmother's stories, which are full of Khmer heritage.

73
00:04:14.067 --> 00:04:15.521
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:16.383 --> 00:04:19.393
Grammar focus: Relative clauses with which.

75
00:04:19.693 --> 00:04:20.915
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:21.617 --> 00:04:24.510
Writing, which I love, helps me express myself.

77
00:04:25.417 --> 00:04:27.811
Painting, which is my hobby, relaxes me.

78
00:04:28.717 --> 00:04:31.192
I write poems, which my friends enjoy.

79
00:04:32.133 --> 00:04:37.607
Put commas around a 'which' clause when it adds extra information. Use 'which' for things, not people.

80
00:04:38.350 --> 00:04:42.070
Be careful! Don't say: Writing, that I love, helps me.

81
00:04:44.033 --> 00:04:46.695
Say: Writing, which I love, helps me.

82
00:04:46.995 --> 00:04:49.041
Use 'which', not 'that', after a comma.

83
00:04:49.833 --> 00:04:52.486
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:54.580
Finding My Voice.

85
00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:57.866
Creative writing gives me a voice to share my perspective.

86
00:04:58.867 --> 00:05:02.701
Poetry, which I discovered at fourteen, is my favourite medium.

87
00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:07.348
I find inspiration in symbolism, like the lotus flower.

88
00:05:08.333 --> 00:05:11.529
Every reader has a different interpretation of my poems.

89
00:05:12.533 --> 00:05:15.752
Authenticity and originality matter more than perfection.

90
00:05:16.867 --> 00:05:20.636
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:21.483 --> 00:05:24.447
Writing, blank I love, helps me relax.

92
00:05:24.747 --> 00:05:27.738
A, which. B, who. C, what.

93
00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:32.940
The answer is A: which.

94
00:05:34.083 --> 00:05:36.257
Being new and not copied is blank.

95
00:05:36.557 --> 00:05:40.849
A, originality. B, symbolism. C, narrative.

96
00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:46.504
The answer is A: originality.

97
00:05:47.650 --> 00:05:50.880
A material or way used to create art is a blank.

98
00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:54.776
A, medium. B, voice. C, perspective.

99
00:05:58.333 --> 00:06:00.321
The answer is A: medium.

100
00:06:01.533 --> 00:06:04.731
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:06:05.583 --> 00:06:07.896
How do you express yourself creatively?

102
00:06:16.683 --> 00:06:18.381
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:18.681 --> 00:06:28.624
I express myself through drawing, which I have loved since I was small. Drawing, which relaxes me, also helps me share my feelings.

104
00:06:28.924 --> 00:06:31.145
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:32.050 --> 00:06:36.572
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and relative clauses with which.

106
00:06:36.872 --> 00:06:40.859
Today's value is creativity. Use your imagination when you play.

107
00:06:41.159 --> 00:06:43.440
See you in Unit two. Goodbye!

108
00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:47.507
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

